{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600186",
      "title": "Working with Multiple State Properties",
      "sourceHash": "586ed5e18f5fea461d732da2cfda92287208ddf76f0e6de90bbab87deb873edf",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.6,
          "en": "So now we already learned quite a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.6,
          "end": 6.91,
          "en": "about Redux but up to this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.91,
          "end": 10.96,
          "en": "we always just worked with our single counter value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.96,
          "end": 13.6,
          "en": "Now I got this Toggle Counter button here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.6,
          "end": 14.71,
          "en": "and when it's clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.71,
          "end": 17.09,
          "en": "I wanna make sure that the counter is hidden",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.09,
          "end": 19.71,
          "en": "and when it's clicked again, it should be shown again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.71,
          "end": 23.253,
          "en": "Now for this, of course, we could use useState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.113,
          "end": 27.42,
          "en": "So we could set up some local state in this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.42,
          "end": 31.4,
          "en": "which we manage with useState, not with Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.4,
          "end": 34.09,
          "en": "And that would be the proper way of doing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.09,
          "end": 37.18,
          "en": "because showing or hiding the counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.18,
          "end": 40.9,
          "en": "is something which only is interesting to this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.9,
          "end": 44.08,
          "en": "not to any other part of the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.08,
          "end": 46.99,
          "en": "but the same could be set about our counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.99,
          "end": 50.41,
          "en": "We are only using the counter in this component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.41,
          "end": 53.66,
          "en": "So the counter technically also is local state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.56,
          "end": 57.4,
          "en": "but this is just a simple demo to get started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.4,
          "end": 61.54,
          "en": "So let's assume that both the counter as well as the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.54,
          "end": 63.93,
          "en": "wherever the counter should be visible or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.93,
          "end": 66.94,
          "en": "is a global state which is also the interesting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.94,
          "end": 70.53999999999999,
          "en": "to other components even though that's not the case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.53999999999999,
          "end": 73.2,
          "en": "As we progress once we know these basics,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.2,
          "end": 76.53,
          "en": "we will, of course, also work on demos and projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.53,
          "end": 79.27,
          "en": "where this then really is the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.27,
          "end": 81.82,
          "en": "But for the moment, let's assume it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.82,
          "end": 83.56,
          "en": "So when we click this button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.56,
          "end": 86.52,
          "en": "the toggleCounterHandler is fired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.52,
          "end": 89.9,
          "en": "And then here we wanna dispatch an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.9,
          "end": 92.72,
          "en": "which changes some state in Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.72,
          "end": 96.263,
          "en": "which controls whether this counter div is shown or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.91,
          "end": 101.08,
          "en": "For this, we need to add a new state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.08,
          "end": 105.4,
          "en": "a new piece of data to our Redux store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.4,
          "end": 108.31,
          "en": "And how do we now do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.31,
          "end": 110.75,
          "en": "Well, to add a new piece of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.75,
          "end": 114.91,
          "en": "we need to go to our reducer in the end and just add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.91,
          "end": 119.91,
          "en": "to all these state snapshots which we are producing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.05,
          "end": 122.75,
          "en": "Let's start with the initial state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.75,
          "end": 125.37,
          "en": "When we start besides having a counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.37,
          "end": 129.5,
          "en": "which has a value of zero, I wanna have a showCounter field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.5,
          "end": 134.23,
          "en": "which has a value of true or false, that's up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.23,
          "end": 135.98,
          "en": "And to keep this a bit more readable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.98,
          "end": 138.97,
          "en": "I'll extract that and store that in a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.97,
          "end": 142.52,
          "en": "named initialState like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.52,
          "end": 145.07999999999998,
          "en": "and assign initialState here then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.07999999999998,
          "end": 147.223,
          "en": "just to make this a bit easier to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.37,
          "end": 152.79,
          "en": "Now when we increment, we are changing the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.79,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "we don't care about showCounter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 160.49,
          "en": "We still need to set the showCounter property here though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.55,
          "end": 164.49,
          "en": "because we are returning the overall state object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 168.72,
          "en": "and Redux won't merge your changes with the existing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.72,
          "end": 170.99,
          "en": "It instead takes what you return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.99,
          "end": 174.36,
          "en": "and replaces the existing state with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.36,
          "end": 176.35,
          "en": "More on that in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.35,
          "end": 178.54,
          "en": "But for the moment that's just accept it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.54,
          "end": 183.08,
          "en": "and set showCounter here to state.showCounter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.08,
          "end": 185.97,
          "en": "So to the value we currently have in our state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.97,
          "end": 188.48,
          "en": "because for increment, we don't wanna change it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.48,
          "end": 192.263,
          "en": "so we will just take the existing showCounter value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.67,
          "end": 196.51,
          "en": "And then we can do the same here for increase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.51,
          "end": 198.32999999999998,
          "en": "because there we also wanna keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.32999999999998,
          "end": 201.23,
          "en": "the existing showCounter value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.23,
          "end": 204.173,
          "en": "and do the same for decrement here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.78,
          "end": 209.65,
          "en": "But now I will also handle a new action type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.65,
          "end": 212.7,
          "en": "and by the way, since we have many if statements here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.7,
          "end": 215.67000000000002,
          "en": "we could also use a switch case statement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.67000000000002,
          "end": 218.9,
          "en": "but I will stick to multiple if statements here for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.9,
          "end": 221.31,
          "en": "and in this new action type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.31,
          "end": 224.7,
          "en": "I will check for, let's say toggle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.7,
          "end": 227.7,
          "en": "Now the identifier just like all these identifiers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 227.7,
          "end": 228.95,
          "en": "is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.95,
          "end": 233.18,
          "en": "I'll go with toggle and then return a new object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.18,
          "end": 236.54,
          "en": "Here, we now wanna change showCounter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.54,
          "end": 240.1,
          "en": "and set it to the opposite of what it was before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.1,
          "end": 243.04,
          "en": "If it was true, we wanna set it to false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.04,
          "end": 245.96,
          "en": "if it was false, we wanna set it to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.96,
          "end": 249.08,
          "en": "And we can do this by simply adding an exclamation mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 249.08,
          "end": 251.9,
          "en": "and then accessing state.showCounter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.9,
          "end": 254.023,
          "en": "This will invert the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.89,
          "end": 258.01,
          "en": "Now for the counter itself, we wanna keep the existing state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.01,
          "end": 261.01,
          "en": "because we don't wanna change this here for this action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 261.01,
          "end": 263.593,
          "en": "So we just set counter to state.counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 265.66,
          "end": 269.52,
          "en": "Now we also support this new toggle action type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.52,
          "end": 274.29,
          "en": "and hence back in counter.js in the toggleCounterHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.29,
          "end": 276.92,
          "en": "we should dispatch such an action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.92,
          "end": 281.193,
          "en": "We dispatch a new action object where the type is toggle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 283.84000000000003,
          "end": 287.90999999999997,
          "en": "Now we can take advantage of this toggle state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 287.90999999999997,
          "end": 290.36,
          "en": "so of the show counter.state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 290.36,
          "end": 292.63,
          "en": "and for that we need to get access to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.63,
          "end": 297.3,
          "en": "So all to in the counter, we again call useSelector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 297.3,
          "end": 300.91,
          "en": "We can use this multiple times to retrieve different pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 300.91,
          "end": 302.94,
          "en": "of data from the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 302.94,
          "end": 304.81,
          "en": "And here I'm then interested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 304.81,
          "end": 308.173,
          "en": "in my showCounter piece of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 309.17,
          "end": 312.57,
          "en": "and I'll store that in a show constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 312.57,
          "end": 314.62,
          "en": "The constant name of course is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 315.75,
          "end": 318.19,
          "en": "Now again, that will then always update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 318.19,
          "end": 320.71,
          "en": "and the component will be re-evaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 320.71,
          "end": 324.4,
          "en": "whenever that data which we're accessing here changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 324.4,
          "end": 327.76,
          "en": "So now here with show extracted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 327.76,
          "end": 331.9,
          "en": "we now can render this div here conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.9,
          "end": 335.13,
          "en": "by checking if show and only rendering the div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 335.13,
          "end": 338.98,
          "en": "if show is truthy, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 338.98,
          "end": 341.27,
          "en": "If we now save this and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 341.27,
          "end": 343.34000000000003,
          "en": "if we click Toggle Counter, it's gone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 343.34000000000003,
          "end": 345.73,
          "en": "if I click this again, it's there again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 345.73,
          "end": 348.52,
          "en": "I can still increase it even if it's hidden",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 348.52,
          "end": 350.32,
          "en": "but it only shows up when,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 350.32,
          "end": 352.69,
          "en": "well, when I click Toggle Counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 352.69,
          "end": 356.2,
          "en": "So that now also works and that is how we can manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 356.2,
          "end": 361.03,
          "en": "multiple different pieces of data in our state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 361.03,
          "end": 364.37,
          "en": "Of course, this data is still kind of connected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 364.37,
          "end": 365.853,
          "en": "we have the counter and then the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 365.853,
          "end": 368.06,
          "en": "whether we wanna show it or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 368.06,
          "end": 370.52,
          "en": "but it's too totally different values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 370.52,
          "end": 373.47,
          "en": "which are changed in totally different ways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 373.47,
          "end": 375.57,
          "en": "So therefore, that is how we can manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 375.57,
          "end": 377.463,
          "en": "multiple pieces of data.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}